{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when Isaac was old.</b> The reason for this notification is that this was the cause whereby Jacob would take the blessings without him recognizing him. And the language conveys distress, that Jacob was forced to take the blessings by means of this cause and not with Isaac's knowledge, for from this many causes of suffering were brought about for the children of our nation." "<b>et Esau.</b> And it does not say ״to Esau,״ for he could not see him to say that he called him; rather, he called his name." "<b>his elder son.</b> This gives the reason why he did not call Jacob, for this one was the firstborn — and perhaps he did not know the difference. And the reason of Isaac, that he desired to bless Esau the wicked, is that he thought that through the power of the blessings he would turn to the quality of good and improve his ways, for the righteous agonize when their children do evil, and he would exert himself with him to improve him, and it is possible that it would have been effective. And you will find that they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 76:9), that Jacob was punished for withholding Dinah from Esau, for it is possible that she would have turned him to the better — see, then, that it was possible for him to turn to the better."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:41.287924944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}